; Maze 4 map (24 x 32 tile codes)
;
; Maze 4 map, the fourth maze (maze number 3). Map of tile codes, 24 rows of 32 columns, one byte per character cell,
; row by row (768 bytes = SCREEN_ROWS x SCREEN_COLS). #R$6B75 (DrawMaze) draws the whole map from the top-left of the
; screen; row 0 is empty in every maze and is overwritten by the status line (#R$7C47) or the demo banner (#R$6AE7).
; Tile codes (the graphics are the 8-byte entries of #R$7BF7, index = code):
;  0 empty floor (TILE_EMPTY), drawn yellow-on-white; this is where Horace and the guards walk
;  1 horizontal wall (two parallel lines)
;  2 flower (TILE_FLOWER), green; worth 10 points
;  3 arrow pointing right (TILE_ARROW), black; the left-hand arrows are where Horace enters (he cannot move into them
;   again), the right-hand ones are the exit to the next maze
;  4 vertical wall (two parallel lines)
;  5 wall corner, top-left; 6 top-right; 7 bottom-left; 8 bottom-right (all walls are cyan)
;  9 wrap pad (TILE_BLANK_WHITE): a blank cell drawn white on white, so invisible; going up or down into it moves the
;   walker by the vertical wrap delta of the maze descriptor (#R$6FCF)
; After drawing, the game never reads the map again: walls, flowers and arrows are recognised from the screen
; attributes ($3D, $3C, $38; #R$6CC2).
; .
; Occupies rows 2-22. Entrance arrows in column 0, rows 3-4, where Horace starts; exit arrows in column 31, rows
; 20-21. Eight wrap pads (tile 9): rows 3 and 21, columns 4-5 and 26-27. 24 flowers.
; Its descriptor is #R$6FEF (Maze4Desc). #R$6000 selects the map by the maze number in #R$7C63 and draws it with
; #R$6B75. The four maps are not stored in game order: this one is maze number 3.
;
@label=Maze4Map
